60,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate A is a central repository. It fits the standardization gap.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Candidate B is a shared tool. It might use the software allowance.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Sakura,,Candidate D is a field app. The network coverage is a problem.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Candidate A addresses the duplicate address issue directly.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate B might reduce the manual notes the coordination group writes.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Ryuji, yes. A fixes the root cause of the misrouted deliveries.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Sakura, D is risky if the signal is down for afternoons.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Daisuke, correct. The visitor device approval also took six weeks.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, B drafts summaries, but does it require daily entry from everyone?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, if it reads task boards, it might be passive. That is good.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Servas,,Candidate C is training videos. The last rollouts show narrow tools survive.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"C is fixed-fee production work. The cost is stable, unlike licences.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Sakura,,C doesn't depend on customer plant networks. It is safer technically.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,C doesn't fix the daily copying loss. It is a nice-to-have.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,C adds work to the coordination group to manage the studio.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for A. It solves the data duplication and has a clear owner.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for A. It uses the software allowance and avoids licence creep.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Sakura,,I vote for A. It avoids the network risks of D and the staffing of C.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for A. It directly addresses the time lost to copying records.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I vote for A. It reduces the manual burden on the coordination group.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
